            {
                "entry_id": "8f0a4b8b-d551-31c6-aa76-c6bd9da0356a",
                "word": "Dorian",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ab856da7-fefd-4248-9838-a891c11bbe52",
                        "entry_id": "8f0a4b8b-d551-31c6-aa76-c6bd9da0356a",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Dorian"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "879cb6ef-1047-4a97-82dd-c01c13330e8d",
                        "entry_id": "8f0a4b8b-d551-31c6-aa76-c6bd9da0356a",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Dorian"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5bef7339-90ff-3c8a-92d2-fc7a773da3f2",
                        "entry_id": "8f0a4b8b-d551-31c6-aa76-c6bd9da0356a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the Dorians."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                        "entry_id": "8f0a4b8b-d551-31c6-aa76-c6bd9da0356a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Homosexual, gay; preferring exclusively men as romantic or sexual partners; male counterpart of lesbian."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a man"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ad9ed04-bed3-4d28-8ea4-944b3d0f7b90",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "while the [Dorian] love of males for males in Greece obtained moralisation, and reached the high position of a recognised social function, the [Lesbian] love of female for female remained undeveloped and unhonoured"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3bfe516-0b43-4f0b-a7f5-e49ff32a9df7",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "All the Spartan kings and generals grew up under the institution of Dorian love. Epameinondas and Alexander were notable lovers; and the names of their comrades are recorded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a57826f-b2cc-4cc4-a630-12d85df72b82",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "And the evidence from Symonds's Memoirs seems to suggest that 'Ionian' implied pederastic relations, as attested in ancient Athens, whereas 'Dorian' involved two virile men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "233d130f-0332-41e1-84c5-4645ec9ca12e",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "Dorian love, on the other hand, was a love between two virile equals, and so exceptional and unique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a768f083-3ef4-4333-b6f7-bbbe7ca7d94f",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "Gay may not be ideal, and it has acquired negative connotations in recent years. I'd much prefer the beautiful word, Dorian, which can be both noun and adjective."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f71bf91-f2fd-4a1a-9af4-cfa4b6f7514a",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "Wilde’s choice for his main protagonist’s name a “veiled reference to ‘Dorian’ or ‘Greek’ love”."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bef78edd-f36f-475d-b04d-26307e8c33ce",
                                "sense_id": "ded97d8e-00df-3264-a566-697b3210ed5c",
                                "text": "\"Dorian love\" between two masculine adult men should now be seen as a model for modern democratic, socialist politics."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
